<title>CHILE: Entel March international traffic rises.</title>
<headline>Entel March international traffic rises.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Entel Chile posted a sharp increase in its international long-distance traffic in March compared with its market share in the previous three months, said the Telecommunications Subsecretariat.</p>
<p>Entel carried 36 percent of international traffic in the deregulated multicarrier service in March, up from 33 percent in the December-February quarter.</p>
<p>The company's share of national long-distance traffic remained unchanged at 41 percent. The following are the market share figures for March for the eight carriers taking part in the system.</p>
<p> Company		  National	 International</p>
<p> Entel		   41.36	    36.35</p>
<p>CTC Mundo		32.46	    20.85</p>
<p>Chilesat		 16.47	    16.31</p>
<p>VTR			 3.90	    11.02</p>
<p>BellSouth		 1.52	     9.01</p>
<p>Transam		   1.62	     2.96</p>
<p>CNT Carrier	     2.43	     0.98</p>
<p>Iusatel		   0.24	     2.52</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
